  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1059 AM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nA shortwave will move through overnight Friday into Saturday, \nbringing medium to high rain and storm chances back into the \nforecast. The bulk of the activity looks to occur in the morning\nhours of Saturday with activity lingering into the afternoon. \nSevere weather is not expected, but some episodes of heavy rain \nwill be possible as PWATs climb back above 2\", leading to a \nlocalized flooding threat. Instability is very little since there \nwill be so much cloud contamination by the time we reach the peak \nheating hours of the day. Activity will wind down late Saturday.\nSunday is looking dry and hot with highs in the low 90s. An \nexpansive area of high pressure aloft will be the dominant \nforecast feature next week, sending temperatures up and minimizing\nrain chances. Moderate HeatRisk is likely by Tuesday, which will \nbe the hottest day of the week as highs reach into the mid to \nupper 90s, so be thinking about this if you have any outdoor \ninterests. Take frequent breaks in a cool place, and stay \nhydrated. As Middle TN remains fixed on the eastern fringes of the\nhigh aloft, this will allow for weak shortwaves to filter in, \nkeeping daily low rain and storm chances in with a focus during \nthe afternoon. Chances range from 10-30%. Highs will level off in \nthe low to mid 90s for the remainder of the week.",
